ey = 19 + 22 = 41\n- Logic is sound \u2713\n\n**Agent 6Nkg (Programming Expert):**\n- Code correctly defines variables: spent_books = 6, spent_pens = 16, remaining_money = 19\n- Correctly calculates total_spent = spent_books + spent_pens\n- Correctly calculates original_money = remaining_money + total_spent\n- Returns 41\n- Code corresponds to the solution analysis \u2713\n\nBoth the analysis and code are correct and consistent with each other.\n\nThe answer is 41"], "Math Solver99RW": ["The answer is 41"]}], "Response": ["The problem is straightforward: Edward spent $6 on books and $16 on pens, totaling $22 in spending. After spending, he has $19 left. Therefore, the amount he had before spending is $19 + $22 = $41.\n\nThe answer is 41"], "Attempt answer": "41", "Solved": true, "Total solved": 11, "Total executed": 12, "Accuracy": 0.9166666666666666}
